{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ag, sorry, this computer is still thinking. Please sit, I will be with you just now.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Good afternoon, doctor. Thank you for seeing me. The robot on Main Road was out, so I was anxious I might be late.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): You are fine, you are here. What has been troubling you?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): It is a spinning feeling, doctor. It comes when I turn in bed, and also when I look up.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Spinning. Sorry, say that again, I was on the wrong screen.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Certainly. If I roll onto my side in bed, or if I tip my head to look up, the room spins. It lasts only a few seconds, and then it passes.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long has this been going on?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Since last week. Well, actually, I cannot pin the exact day. It may have been the Monday, or the day after the long weekend.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Last week, more or less. Does anything else come with the spinning?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Nausea, doctor. I feel distinctly queasy while it is happening, and the queasiness fades as the spinning fades.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): And when did that queasiness start?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): That I cannot date. Since Diwali, or after, I think. Though I may be mixing it up with last week. I truly cannot say.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Any pain in the ears?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No, doctor. There is no ear pain.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): And your hearing, has it dropped on either side?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I have not had any hearing loss. It is as it has always been.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. The screen has frozen again. Have you had a fever with this?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No, doctor. No fever at all.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any cough?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No cough.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): What about passing water, any burning or trouble there?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, I am not sure I should say yes. Perhaps once, but I think that was only the heat, and I cannot really say there is a problem.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): We will leave that. What tablets are you on?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Only enalapril, doctor. Ten milligrams every morning, for my blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, ten or twenty? This note is tiny and I lost my place.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten milligrams. I am quite sure of that. One tablet each morning.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any bad reaction to a medicine in the past? Rash, swelling, trouble breathing?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No, never. I have taken penicillin, and everything of that sort. Amoxacylin, for a tooth some years back, and I was perfectly well on it.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): No reactions, then. Your blood pressure treatment can stay as it is. I will not add another tablet. Let me examine you, if this thing will let me type.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Of course, doctor. I am in your hands.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Onto the couch, please. I am going to do a positional test. I turn your head and lie you back quickly. It may set the spin off for a moment.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): I understand. Please go ahead.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right side first. Head turned, and down. There. Did it come?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, doctor. That was the same spinning, only a few seconds. It is easing already.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): I saw a short burst of flickering in the eyes, torsional, and then it died away. Other side now.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): That side felt quite ordinary. No spinning that time.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Left side is quiet. No nystagmus. Sit up slowly. Shame, I know that was horrid.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Thank you. It has settled, doctor.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): I think this is benign positional vertigo. The little crystals in the inner ear shift when you move your head, and that is what sets the spin off. The test just now fits with that.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): I see. Is it a serious matter?",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): Not in the dangerous sense. It is thoroughly unpleasant, but we treat it with a manoeuvre and with exercises, not with more medicine. I am not prescribing anything new today.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): That is a relief. What should I do at home?",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): I will teach you the Brandt-Daroff exercise. Sit, then lie quickly onto one side, stay until the spin stops and a little longer, sit up, then do the other side. Three times a day, until it quietens. And do not drive if you are still spinning.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Three times a day. I shall do it carefully. I lecture at the university in the mornings, so I will fit it in before I leave the house.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): Good. If you feel unsteady on the stairs there, hold the rail. Come back and see me in two weeks and we will see how it stands.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): In two weeks. Thank you, doctor. May I continue the enalapril exactly as before?",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yes. Carry on with the enalapril, ten milligrams in the morning. Do not stop it. Reception will book those two weeks. I must save this before it crashes."
 ],
